{
  "format": 1,
  "doc": "Canonical golden-frame cases for /ws/reader-sync (#210). Every implementation adapter drives its in-process session core through `steps` and must emit the exact frame sequence in each `expect`. Dynamic values use @bindings harvested from received frames: @<link>.link, @<link>.member, @<link>.token, @session, @code, @digest, @leader.member, @follower.member, @manifest.canonical (canonical JSON text of the case's resolver manifest; single-chunk cases only). Ops: link/send/expect/drain/detach/tick. Every client request carries the full request envelope {v, requestId, sessionId, workEpoch, baseRevision, type, payload} — lifecycle ops use sessionId:null workEpoch:0 baseRevision:0. requestIds must be unique within a case: .member/.token bindings resolve the sending link by requestId alone, so a second link reusing an id mis-attributes. tick is currently py-adapter-only — the rs adapter panics on it (real-clock core), so cases must not use it until both sides implement it.",
  "resolver": {
    "work": {
      "folder": "work",
      "offset": 0,
      "chapters": [
        {"name": "c0", "folder": "work",
         "pages": ["p001.png", "p002.png", "p003.png", "p004.png", "p005.png"]}
      ]
    }
  },
